  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Description":          "Audio Scene Manager: acquires audio, edits it into Objects, composes Objects into a Scene, and delivers the Scene. UNLIKE MMC-AMQ and MMC-TST, acquisition and delivery ARE SubAIMs here, and legitimately so: CAE-AOA and CAE-ASD sit at a HARDWARE boundary, capturing and rendering an environment rather than interacting with the user. Nothing here would travel with the User Agent if the User Agent became remote - the microphones stay with the scene. The User Agent's part is what the figure shows: User Commands and the listener's Point of View. Each user action is one Command on a UserCommand Port, so an interactive session is a sequence of runs, with the state between them held in Shared Storage.",

